# Preserve limb bend-plane orientation and body-relative twist

Status: DONE
Milestone: Correct imported-avatar hip collapse in default constrained live mode
Dependencies: 13_BLENDER_MODEL_RUNTIME.todo, 20_CORE_MOTION_UPGRADE.todo

## Purpose
Repair the runtime limb-frame mismatch behind the reported hourglass hip and broken rear turns.
Do not compensate by widening geometry, changing GLB weights or bypassing missing-data visibility.

## Tasks
- [x] Reproduce with the reported current GLB and actual enhanced/world/constrained options.
- [x] Confirm a 180-degree thigh-frame error on observations made from the asset's own rest joints.
- [x] Align reference and solved cross-product conventions.
- [x] Preserve ancestor-relative rotation for unconstrained limb/hand/foot aiming.
- [x] Transport near-straight bend-plane history in the body frame.
- [x] Add failing-before rest, full-turn, leaning and temporal regression tests.
- [x] Run focused tests, the full current suite and targeted Ruff checks.
- [x] Complete same-detection recording comparison and native Studio checks.
- [x] Record source hashes, aggregate evidence and application-restart guidance.

## Acceptance criteria
- [x] Bent and straight fixture rigs recover their authored frames in neutral pose.
- [x] Rigid body turns/leans preserve bone lengths and do not cancel pelvis/thigh skin matrices.
- [x] Turning while nearly straight does not leave the remembered bend plane camera-fixed.
- [x] Existing loss, interpolation, face controls and import behavior remain covered.
- [x] The same provided GLB is checked in the native application with no model replacement.

## Completion evidence
- tests\test_rig_twist.py; focused tests include tests\test_rig_motion.py.
- Private diagnostic work in the Blender3DModels production workspace; no user media or
